WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.055 --> 00:00:06.427
Ivy was sitting with Ezra and Glen at morning assembly.

2
00:00:06.429 --> 00:00:11.961
"Listen up!" Private said. "Sports Day is next week.

3
00:00:11.962 --> 00:00:18.278
There will be relay races, swimming competitions, and a basketball free throw.

4
00:00:18.279 --> 00:00:24.076
We'll also have a canoe race and a home run derby."

5
00:00:24.077 --> 00:00:31.055
Ivy groaned. "Why aren't there any drawing competitions?"

6
00:00:31.056 --> 00:00:34.159
Private asked Mango to announce the prize.

7
00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:39.319
Mango grinned. "All the winners get Frosty Freeze ice cream!"

8
00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:42.234
The campers cheered.

9
00:00:42.235 --> 00:00:46.861
Ezra, Glen, and the others did the crazy Camp Evergreen dance.

10
00:00:46.862 --> 00:00:49.159
Ivy rolled her eyes.

11
00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:56.861
"This prison camp is so bad, the inmates get excited over ice cream," she thought.

12
00:00:56.862 --> 00:01:00.549
Private pointed to the sign-up sheets on the bulletin board.

13
00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:03.078
Everyone rushed to get in line.

14
00:01:03.079 --> 00:01:05.908
Ivy and the boys stood near the back.

15
00:01:05.909 --> 00:01:09.570
"I don't mind relay races," Ezra said.

16
00:01:09.571 --> 00:01:12.151
"I'm actually a fast runner.

17
00:01:12.152 --> 00:01:16.617
I just imagine bullies chasing me for my lunch money." Glen

18
00:01:16.618 --> 00:01:22.438
grinned. "Last year I came in fifth place in swimming." "Fifth?"

19
00:01:22.439 --> 00:01:29.449
Ivy stared at him. "That's not . . . great." "My

20
00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:33.210
swimsuit was too big," Glen said. "So,

21
00:01:33.211 --> 00:01:36.552
I had to hold it up while I swam. It

22
00:01:36.553 --> 00:01:43.564
fits perfectly this year. I'm bound to do better!" Ezra

23
00:01:43.565 --> 00:01:47.426
frowned when they finally reached the sign-up sheets. "What

24
00:01:47.427 --> 00:01:54.617
are we going to do? Almost every event is full." "There

25
00:01:54.618 --> 00:01:58.616
are three openings for the canoe race," Ezra said. Glen

26
00:01:58.617 --> 00:02:04.619
shrugged. "It's not my favorite. But we can do it together." "Fine,"

27
00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:10.419
Ivy snapped. "But there's only one race I want to win." "Huh?"

28
00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:12.834
Glen said. "The

29
00:02:12.835 --> 00:02:17.572
race to get out of here on the last day of camp!" Ivy said. Glen

30
00:02:17.573 --> 00:02:21.596
wrote their names down for the Yellow team. "We'll

31
00:02:21.597 --> 00:02:24.093
need to practice," he said. "We'll

32
00:02:24.094 --> 00:02:27.504
be racing against the Red and Blue teams." As

33
00:02:27.505 --> 00:02:31.350
they walked to the lake, Ivy complained again. "Why

34
00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:35.084
are sports such a big deal at camp? I'm

35
00:02:35.085 --> 00:02:39.930
drawing a graphic novel, Zombie Attack at Camp Nevergreen .

36
00:02:39.931 --> 00:02:42.861
I can draw zombies faster than anyone.

37
00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:46.287
But nobody cares about that skill."

38
00:02:46.288 --> 00:02:49.529
"I don't like sports either," Ezra said.

39
00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:53.907
"But a trip to Frosty Freeze ice cream shop is a big deal."

40
00:02:53.908 --> 00:02:56.001
"Yeah," Glen said.

41
00:02:56.002 --> 00:02:58.985
"They're famous for the Colossal Cone.

42
00:02:58.986 --> 00:03:01.478
It has four scoops of ice cream!"

43
00:03:01.479 --> 00:03:04.819
"And six toppings," Ezra said.

44
00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:07.341
"Wait!" Ivy halted.

45
00:03:07.342 --> 00:03:13.500
"Are you saying the winners get to leave camp for ice cream?" She grinned.

46
00:03:13.501 --> 00:03:17.659
"Now that's what I call a prize!"

47
00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:22.315
*** At the lake Larry sat in a lifeguard chair watching the

48
00:03:22.316 --> 00:03:25.233
swimmers. Other campers paddled in

49
00:03:25.234 --> 00:03:28.737
canoes. Ivy, Glen, and Ezra approached

50
00:03:28.738 --> 00:03:32.097
Penelope. She was supervising the

51
00:03:32.098 --> 00:03:36.550
canoers. "We need to practice for the canoe race on Sports Day," Glen said.

52
00:03:36.551 --> 00:03:40.639
"Great! How much canoeing have you done?" Penelope asked.

53
00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:43.800
"I did some last year," Glen said.

54
00:03:43.801 --> 00:03:47.173
Ezra nodded. "Me too."

55
00:03:47.174 --> 00:03:51.459
"Well, I've never been in a canoe," Ivy said.

56
00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:55.237
"Time to get started," Penelope said.

57
00:03:55.238 --> 00:04:00.540
The kids gathered paddles and life vests from a shed.

58
00:04:00.541 --> 00:04:04.057
"You'll do a dunk test first," Penelope said.

59
00:04:04.058 --> 00:04:07.188
"Go out on the lake and turn your canoe over.

60
00:04:07.189 --> 00:04:12.867
Then climb back in and paddle back to shore."

61
00:04:12.868 --> 00:04:15.679
An empty canoe was tied to the dock.

62
00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:21.911
The kids got in and started paddling.

63
00:04:21.912 --> 00:04:27.444
Ivy was confused. "Why are we falling out of the canoe on purpose?"

64
00:04:27.445 --> 00:04:30.738
"It's a safety exercise," Glen said.

65
00:04:30.739 --> 00:04:34.530
"Everyone needs to know how to get back in the boat if it capsizes."

66
00:04:34.531 --> 00:04:41.774
Ivy groaned. "I'm ready to get out right now!"

